 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+<a id="req-vet-003"></a>
+
+Staff also ask the inverse question: which veterinarians hold a given specialty. A separate, read-only specialty directory answers it by listing every specialty the clinic knows, each with the veterinarians holding it `[REQ-VET-003]`. All specialties appear on one page rather than a page at a time. The page is reached by its address alone; no other page links to it, and the shared navigation carries no entry for it.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every specialty is listed by its stored name on a single page.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty held by veterinarians, when the specialty directory is opened, then each holder is listed beneath it by first name, then last name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the specialty directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on the page.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty no veterinarian holds is still listed, with no veterinarian beneath it.
+2. A veterinarian holding several specialties appears under each of them.
+3. Specialties, and the veterinarians under each, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+
 ### Language
 
 <a id="req-lang-001"></a><a id="req-lang-002"></a>
